Call-site Target directly on a stdlib call. At run time strconv.ParseBool only fails
with &NumError{Err: ErrSyntax}: sentinel strconv.ErrSyntax under
*strconv.NumError.Unwrap must be present. With the Go 1.27 stdlib the conversion goes
through strconv.toError, a switch over internal/strconv constants the tool does not
decide, so ErrRange, the base/bitSize errors and a bare internal/strconv.Error are
also listed (over-approximation, not a missing origin).
